      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK bunches more comments...\n\nI have made a bunch of suggestions on MEM_COMP names.\n\nWe really need to totally eradicate the old \"pool\" stuff. It only obfuscates memory allocation.\n\nThere are several places we need to add MEM_COMP parameters to functions so they can allocate memory for the correct component (and then any corresponding free/release functions also need the parameter).\n\nIn particular, we need to change the config processing so that we can pass MEM_COMP_EXPORT to it for all export config. There may be other config blocks that also need such.\n\nAt the moment, I think it only makes sense to lump ntirpc into one component, so let\u0027s not change libntirpc at all.\n\nAll that said, I am still wading through so will almost certainly have more comments.",
